<problem>
<name>hasSubpattern</name>
<description>Given a string s, return true if it is possible to split the string into two non-empty substrings such that every character in the first substring appears in the second substring, and vice versa.</description>

<example>
<name>Example 1</name>
<description>Input: s = "abab", Output: true. Explanation: It is possible to split the string into two substrings where the first substring contains all of the characters in s, and the second substring is empty. Also, it is possible to split the string into two substrings where the first substring contains the first three characters of s, and the second substring is the remaining characters.</description>

<name>Example 2</name>
<description>Input: s = "aba", Output: false. Explanation: It is impossible to split the string into two substrings where the first substring contains all of the characters in the second substring, and vice versa.</description>

<name>Example 3</name>
<description>Input: s = "abcaba", Output: true. Explanation: It is possible to split the string into two substrings where the first substring contains all of the characters in the second substring, and vice versa. The first substring can be "ab", and the second substring can be "caba".</description>

<name>Example 4</name>
<description>Input: s = "abccba", Output: true. Explanation: It is possible to split the string into two substrings where the first substring contains all of the characters in the second substring, and vice versa. The first substring can be "ab", and the second substring can be "cabbacba".</description>

<name>Example 5</name>
