<name>Problem</name>
<description>Given an array of words in Codeland language, sort them lexicographically according to Codeland's unique rules.

The rules are as follows:

1. The first character of a word is the same as the last character of the previous word.

2. The next character of a word is the previous character of the previous word, and the next character of the previous word is the previous character of the previous word, and so on.

3. The last character of a word is the same as the first character of the previous word.

